## 1) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug
Title: Avoid silently renumbering the existing "recreate" exit code

Affected:
- quarkus/runtime/src/main/java/org/keycloak/quarkus/runtime/compatibility/CompatibilityResult.java:30-35

Explanation:
`RECREATE_UPGRADE_EXIT_CODE` changes from `4` to `3`. The value `4` is reused for the new `FEATURE_DISABLED` code.

Anything that checks the literal exit code will now get the wrong answer:
- scripts, CI pipelines or automation written against the previous release;
- an operator image built against the old constant;
- dist tests that assert on `4`.

The worst case is a consumer that treats `4` as "recreate required". It will now take a "feature disabled" result as a valid compatibility decision, and it will not recognise `3` as recreate.

Usages outside this diff (operator job handling, dist tests) are not visible here. Check that every consumer refers to the constant rather than a literal. Also call out the change in the release or migration notes. If backward compatibility matters, keep `4` for recreate and give `FEATURE_DISABLED` a new value.

Proposed fix:
~~~java
int ROLLING_UPGRADE_EXIT_CODE = 0;
int RECREATE_UPGRADE_EXIT_CODE = 3; // document change, update all consumers/tests
int FEATURE_DISABLED = 4;
// and grep for literal "4" / exit-code assertions in operator + dist tests
~~~

## 2) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug
Title: Ensure Profile is initialized before the feature check runs

Affected:
- quarkus/runtime/src/main/java/org/keycloak/quarkus/runtime/cli/command/UpdateCompatibilityCheck.java:46-52
- quarkus/runtime/src/main/java/org/keycloak/quarkus/runtime/cli/command/UpdateCompatibilityMetadata.java:46-52

Explanation:
`Profile.isFeatureEnabled(...)` is called before `validateConfig()`. If the Profile has not yet been configured from the CLI or persisted build options, two things can go wrong:
- `Profile.getInstance()` may be null, which causes an NPE.
- The check may run against a stale or default feature set. In that case it would ignore a `--features=rolling-updates` passed on this invocation.

The commit history ("fix test failure") hints that ordering was fragile here. Verify that the Picocli bootstrap configures the Profile before `run()`. Otherwise, move the check after `validateConfig()`, or explicitly resolve features first.

Proposed fix:
~~~java
@Override
public void run() {
    printPreviewWarning();
    validateConfig();
    if (!Profile.isFeatureEnabled(Profile.Feature.ROLLING_UPDATES)) {
        printFeatureDisabled();
        picocli.exit(CompatibilityResult.FEATURE_DISABLED);
        return;
    }
    ...
}
~~~

## 3) Severity: LOW | Type: Doc
Title: Do not append a fixed `--features` option to user-supplied parameters

Affected:
- docs/guides/templates/kc.adoc:53

Explanation:
The macro always appends `--features=rolling-updates` after `${parameters}`. Users copy these snippets with their own configuration. If that configuration already includes `--features=...`, the command ends up with two `--features` options. With last-wins semantics, the user's other features would be dropped.

Dropped features change the feature set used for compatibility metadata. That can give a misleading compatibility result, or a mismatch between the metadata and the check.

The docs should instead tell users to add `rolling-updates` to their existing feature list.

Proposed fix:
~~~
bin/kc.[sh|bat] update-compatibility ${parameters}
// plus a note: "Add `rolling-updates` to your existing --features list (e.g. --features=<yours>,rolling-updates)."
~~~

## 4) Severity: LOW | Type: Test
Title: Do not overwrite existing enabled features in the test CR

Affected:
- operator/src/test/java/org/keycloak/operator/testsuite/integration/UpgradeTest.java:112-115

Explanation:
`setEnabledFeatures(List.of(ROLLING_UPDATES))` replaces any features already present on the default test Keycloak CR. Any setup that relies on other enabled features is silently lost.

The fix is to merge `rolling-updates` into the existing list instead of replacing it.

Proposed fix:
~~~java
var features = kc.getSpec().getFeatureSpec();
var enabled = new ArrayList<String>(Optional.ofNullable(features.getEnabledFeatures()).orElse(List.of()));
enabled.add(Profile.Feature.ROLLING_UPDATES.getKey());
features.setEnabledFeatures(enabled);
~~~
